[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062154420","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#issuecomment-3062154420","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108491","id":3062154420,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62hMS0","user":{"login":"MewPurPur","id":85438892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NDM4ODky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85438892?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur","html_url":"https://github.com/MewPurPur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T12:32:25Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T12:32:25Z","body":"@KoBeWi is a tween expert.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062154420/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062171805","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#issuecomment-3062171805","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108491","id":3062171805,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62hQid","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T12:35:53Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T12:35:53Z","body":"For timers the order does not really matter, at most it can affect the order of `timeout` signals (which I think is not guaranteed anyway?)\r\n\r\nFor Tweens it does matter. If 2 Tweens are tweening the same property, only the last one is effective. While it's not really intended usage, it's still something that is currently guaranteed.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062171805/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062194077","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#issuecomment-3062194077","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108491","id":3062194077,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62hV-d","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T12:42:30Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T12:42:54Z","body":"> For timers the order does not really matter, at most it can affect the order of `timeout` signals (which I think is not guaranteed anyway?)\r\n\r\nI'm not very familiar with timers, but what about this situation:\r\n\r\n```\r\nschedule timer: end (2 seconds)\r\nschedule timer: start (1 second)\r\nlag spike: 5 seconds\r\ntimer complete: end\r\ntimer complete: start\r\n```\r\n\r\nObviously, this isn't good code design. But as a developer, I'd probably still expect the timers to be executed in order of timeout, even under the effect of lag spikes.\r\nIs this something that is currently considered at all?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062194077/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062720461","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#issuecomment-3062720461","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108491","id":3062720461,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62jWfN","user":{"login":"dementive","id":87823030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODIzMDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87823030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive","html_url":"https://github.com/dementive","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T15:20:27Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T16:06:50Z","body":"It seems like both timers and tweens do actually need to be ordered then.\r\n\r\nFor timers I wouldn't want a user who is currently relying on the order of timeout signals to have their game logic break. The goal here was to just rework the internal data structure I definitely want to avoid making any changes to how things behave for users.\r\n\r\nI can make those ordered again easy I just need to make the erasing ordered. This does mean the erase will be slower than before when it was using the List though. I think it's still a win overall because these get iterated over twice every frame. So should gain more out of the reduction in cache misses than is lost from the slowdown from using the Vector erase.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3062720461/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3063650694","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#issuecomment-3063650694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108491","id":3063650694,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62m5mG","user":{"login":"dementive","id":87823030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3ODIzMDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87823030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive","html_url":"https://github.com/dementive","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dementive/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-11T20:06:39Z","updated_at":"2025-07-11T20:06:39Z","body":"I ran a benchmark and AThousandShips was correct that the Vector is actually slower for `tweens` and `timers` processing than the List because they both have to be ordered, making the Vector erase very slow. These are the results I got benchmarking the List vs Vector:\r\n\r\n```\r\n-- With original List usage --\r\n\r\ntimer count: 1000\r\ntimer time: 0.1 seconds\r\nSceneTree Process Timers time average:  2\r\n\r\ntimer count: 10000\r\ntimer time: 0.1 seconds\r\nSceneTree Process Timers time average:  25\r\n\r\ntimer count: 1000\r\ntimer time: 5 seconds\r\nSceneTree Process Timers time average:  37\r\n\r\ntimer count: 10000\r\ntimer time: 5 seconds\r\nSceneTree Process Timers time average:  153\r\n\r\n\r\n-- With Vector changes --\r\n\r\n\r\ntimer count: 1000\r\ntimer time: 0.1 seconds\r\nSceneTree Process Timers time average:  41\r\n\r\ntimer count: 10000\r\ntimer time: 0.1\r\nSceneTree Process Timers time average:  1740\r\n\r\ntimer count 1000\r\ntimer time: 5 seconds\r\nSceneTree Process Timers time average:  14 \r\n\r\ntimer count: 10000\r\ntimer time: 5 seconds\r\nSceneTree Process Timers time average:  132\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe Vector did work marginally faster with timers that are long but short timers at 0.1 seconds were 70x slower with the Vector so it's not going to work.\r\n\r\nGoing to revert those changes to keep the existing List usage because it does actually seem like the optimal thing to use here. Then this PR will only be the change to the `delete_queue`, which doesn't have the same slow erasing problem that timers and tweens do.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3063650694/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068036685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/108491#issuecomment-3068036685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108491","id":3068036685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc623oZN","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-14T06:44:21Z","updated_at":"2025-07-14T06:44:21Z","body":"3.x already uses a `LocalVector` here for delete queue, but watch for the ordering, there were a lot of PRs here, in some cases it is a lot faster to delete in reverse order.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3068036685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]